From 934f3a8537f50f185a08c5620c1f66d346058888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:24:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/29] resync(oracles): re-derive classic-noise,
 cellrefract186, distortion, dither against authority 61aa869/corpus 0ed489ec

Each package's .mjs generator now derives the corpus revision from
tools/glslcpp/check_corpus.py (REVISION) instead of hardcoding
a024dc3a960cc44af454abc7aebce50456c194e6, and asserts the CPU-authority
import closure at 61aa869 (23 files, up from 22 -- adapters/index.js now
imports adapters/remap.js, confirmed by diffing the authority source
directly) instead of the stale e17dd02 closure. Python materializers
derive the same revision from check_corpus.REVISION and re-emit the
native .inc/.sha256 pairs. No pixel/render-case data changed for any of
these four effects; only provenance metadata (corpus path, upstream
revision, closure hashes/cardinality, node version) moved to the current
authority. test_generated_kernels.cpp literal expectations (kOracleSha256,
kCorpusRevision, kAuthorityNode, kClosureSha256, kSourceRelativePath, the
classic-noise kImportClosureCardinality) are updated to match.

Also adds the missing '#include "noisemaker/effects/median.hpp"' that
test_generated_kernels.cpp needs for noisemaker::effects::bind_median --
introduced at base commit 9edf5fb and breaking the build before any of
this oracle work, unrelated to the corpus/authority resync.
